  "result": "All 5 tests pass (the existing 3 plus the 2 new ones in tests/test_t2.py).\n\n**What I changed** in netgraph/graph.py, keeping the existing adjacency-set design:\n\n- **remove_edge(u, v) -> bool**: validates both nodes, returns False if the edge is absent, otherwise discards it from both adjacency sets, decrements the edge counter, and returns True. Self-loops work since discarding from the same set twice is harmless.\n- **degree(u) -> int**: returns the size of the node's neighbour set. A self-loop appears once in that set, so it counts once as required.\n- **connected_components() -> list[list[int]]**: BFS from each unseen node in ascending order, using the existing deque import. Each component is sorted before being appended, and scanning start nodes in order guarantees components are ordered by their smallest member. Isolated nodes form singleton components.\n\nNo files under tests/ were touched, and the SPEC's public interface is unchanged apart from the three additions.",
